Summary of what was done, combining all 16 JSON-converted functions from `.../10/all.R/` into `.../10_kernsmooth/r2py_kernsmooth/__init__.py`:

- **Imports deduplicated/sorted**: stdlib (`math`, `warnings`, `typing`) → third-party (`numpy`, `scipy.stats`), merging overlapping `from scipy.stats import ...` and `from typing import ...` lines into single statements.
- **Dropped intra-batch local imports** (e.g. `from .bkfe import bkfe`, `from .linbin import linbin`, etc.) since those functions now live in the same file — keeping them would have caused `ModuleNotFoundError` on import.
